"""Leading with AI (Leadership Edition), Session 6: The AI market: models, vendors, and buy, rent or build.  Written 12 November 2026.

Merges the useful parts of Executive Sessions 6 and 7 without maths: who makes models, hosted against open weights, the three routes,
what decides (data location and the law, cost per use, lock-in, vendor survival), benchmarks as someone else's test, data centres in Africa.

Cases (research/*.md): GAP-17 Uganda PDPO and Google (hook and data slide), GAP-09 Sunbird Sunflower (case; AGR-09 for the tour tile),
GAP-12 Jacaranda UlizaLlama (case and tour), HLT-06 Babyl Rwanda (case), GAP-14 Cassava and Nvidia, GAP-15 Microsoft and G42 (data centres),
LGL-06 PwC and TEL-10 Vodacom (route examples), TEL-09 Orange, GAP-06 Absa, AGR-12 ITC Krishi Mitra, MFG-09 Nestle (tour tiles),
GAP-10 Lelapa AI (makers slide).  RTL-06 Kenya Airways from the plan is left out: its point (a board-approved policy) belongs to Session 13.
Demonstration: demo_runs/s06_comparison_runs.md (Claude, fresh subagent session, 6 November 2026, one run; Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct on a laptop,
three runs).  File sizes: demo_runs/s07_sizes_run.md (SmolLM2-135M, 6 November 2026, one run).  The rent and host prices are invented to show
the idea.  Nile Valley Foods is fictional.
"""

